## Overview
#c1[overview,i5] Cobra provides a framework for building Go CLI applications using a hierarchical command-argument-flag pattern, supporting scaffolding via the cobra-cli tool.
  > README.md:7 #d6e07f7e1887
  > README.md::Concepts #61be5fc556df
  > README.md::Usage #5b66dfef7bbf
#c2[overview,i5] The library manages the command lifecycle through a strict execution order of pre-run, run, and post-run hooks, while supporting context propagation and hierarchical configuration lookups.
  > command.go:117-122 #bb4c25112f98
  > command.go::getOut #95340933a26b
  > command.go:266-267 #a228d1abb043
  > command.go:919-922 #3925330d0c8b
  > command.go:1144-1146 #d262bd2e89b7
#c3[overview,i5] Cobra offers robust argument validation and flag management, including support for positional argument validators, flag groups, and custom parsing logic to ensure command-line input integrity.
