  > command.go::AddCommand #194dc973d95b

## (root)
#c8[i5] Cobra is a library designed for creating modern CLI applications in Go, used by projects like Kubernetes, Hugo, and GitHub CLI.
  > README.md:7 #d6e07f7e1887
#c9[i4] Cobra applications follow a command-argument-flag pattern: APPNAME COMMAND ARG --FLAG.
  > README.md::Concepts #61be5fc556df
#c10[i3] Cobra provides automatic shell autocomplete generation for bash, zsh, fish, and powershell.
  > README.md::Overview #311fca062beb
#c11[i3] Cobra offers optional integration with the viper library to support 12-factor applications.
  > README.md::Overview #311fca062beb
#c12[i4] The cobra-cli tool is used to bootstrap application scaffolding and generate command files for Cobra-based applications.
  > README.md::Usage #5b66dfef7bbf
#c13[i2] Cobra is released under the Apache 2.0 license.
  > README.md::License #5f620bbcdf49
#c14[i5] The `AppendActiveHelp` function appends a string prefixed with `_activeHelp_ ` to a completion array, allowing completion scripts to display ActiveHelp to users.
  > active_help.go:31-33 #12bbeda7ed21
#c15[i3] Calling `AppendActiveHelp` multiple times on the same array causes subsequent ActiveHelp lines to appear below previous ones during completion.
  > active_help.go:36-37 #3eb1084001b4
#c16[i5] The `GetActiveHelpConfig` function checks the global environment variable `COBRA_ACTIVE_HELP` first; if set to "0", it disables ActiveHelp regardless of program-specific settings.
  > active_help.go:45-46 #6c44079e63a4
#c17[i4] Program-specific ActiveHelp configuration is retrieved via an environment variable formatted as `<PROGRAM>_ACTIVE_HELP`, where non-ASCII-alphanumeric characters in the root command name are replaced by underscores.
  > active_help.go:56-57 #506bbb6c830f
#c18[i4] The constant `activeHelpMarker` defines the internal prefix `_activeHelp_ ` used to identify ActiveHelp strings within completion arrays.
  > active_help.go:23 #42373e96b248
